## Report

**Task:** Fix `model_to_dict(instance, fields=[])` returning all fields instead of an empty dict (TASK.md).

**Cause:** In `django/forms/models.py`, `model_to_dict()` used a truthy check — `if fields and f.name not in fields:` — so an empty `fields=[]` list was treated the same as `None` ("no restriction") and every field was included.

**Fix (minimal, one line, in source not tests):** line 86 of `django/forms/models.py`:
```diff
-        if fields and f.name not in fields:
+        if fields is not None and f.name not in fields:
